.\" Manpage for install.sh
.TH INSTALL 1 "August 2024" "1.0" "Bash Scripts"
.SH NAME
install.sh \- Manage installation of bash scripts into ~/.local/bin/
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B install.sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B install.sh
script provides a TUI (Text User Interface) for managing the installation, removal, and update of bash scripts from the repository. It also handles installation of manpages and Zsh completions from the `misc/` directory.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.TP
.B dialog
.SH USAGE
To run the script manager:
.PP
.B ./install.sh
.PP
The main menu includes options to:
.TP
.B Install Scripts
Lists available scripts for installation, excluding those already installed. Checks for and optionally installs associated manpages.
.TP
.B List Installed Scripts
Displays currently installed scripts in `~/.local/bin/`.
.TP
.B Remove Scripts
Allows removal of installed scripts and their associated manpages.
.TP
.B Update Scripts from Repo
Pulls the latest updates from the repository.
.TP
.B Install Zsh Completions
Installs Zsh completions from `misc/` into `~/.zsh/completions/`.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 1 if an error occurs or if dependencies are missing.
.SH AUTHOR
AnAnnoyinGoose

